 null, 'Kussmaul breathing is a compensatory response to severe metabolic acidosis (classically diabetic ketoacidosis), increasing ventilation to blow off CO2 and raise blood pH.'),
('NEET PG', 'Clinical Medicine and Allied', 'General Medicine', 'hard', 'mcq',
 'Which antibiotic is a preferred first-line treatment for typhoid fever, especially where fluoroquinolone resistance is common?',
