 null, 'Ceftriaxone, a third-generation cephalosporin, is widely used for typhoid fever, particularly given rising fluoroquinolone resistance in Salmonella Typhi.'),
('NEET PG', 'Clinical Medicine and Allied', 'General Medicine', 'hard', 'mcq',
 'The most common cause of nephrotic syndrome in children is:',
 '[{"text":"Minimal change disease","isCorrect":true},{"text":"Membranous nephropathy","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Focal segmental glomerulosclerosis","isCorrect":false},{"text":"IgA nephropathy","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb,
 null, 'Minimal change disease is the most common cause of nephrotic syndrome in children, typically presenting with steroid-responsive proteinuria and normal-appearing glomeruli on light microscopy.'),

